            <ArticleTitle>Enhanced solar absorption and visible-light photocatalytic and photoelectrochemical properties of aluminium-reduced BaTiO3 nanoparticles.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc07636c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Enhanced solar light absorption and photocatalytic and photoelectrochemical properties have been achieved in black BaTiO3 with a unique core/shell structure (crystalline BaTiO3@amorphous BaTiO3-x) using an Al-reduction method. This finding may open a new avenue to tune the inert ferroelectric materials toward excellent photocatalysts for advanced applications.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
